An independent KMIP implementation. It is not endorsed or certified by OASIS.

Numeric tag/operation/enumeration registries are extracted from the OASIS KMIP
specifications. The standards and official test case documents remain copyright
OASIS Open and subject to their own notices. Source URLs, editions and hashes are
recorded in docs/specs/. Downloaded documents are not relicensed by this project.

Interoperability tests fetch separately licensed software from OVH, Thales/
Gemalto, OpenKMIP and NLnetLabs. Their copyrights and licenses remain with their
respective owners. No client SDK implementation is included in the server image.
See interop/clients.lock.json and the client Cargo/Go/Python lock files.

The server uses OpenSSL and dependencies listed in Cargo.lock. Their licenses
apply independently. The container image is built from Red Hat Universal Base
Image 9 (ubi-micro) and contains Red Hat RPM packages (glibc, libgcc, OpenSSL,
the RHEL 9 OpenSSL FIPS provider, crypto-policies, zlib and base filesystem
packages). Their license texts are shipped under /usr/share/licenses in the
image. Redistribution of the UBI content is subject to the Red Hat Universal
Base Image End User License Agreement:
https://www.redhat.com/en/about/red-hat-end-user-license-agreements#UBI

Numerical ECDSA verification values in tests/ec-rfc6979.json are taken from
RFC 6979 (T. Pornin, IETF Trust, 2013). The RFC text and its sample implementation
are not included. These tests do not claim deterministic signature generation.

Numerical HMAC known-answer values in tests/stream_crypto.rs are from RFC 4231
(M. Nystrom, The Internet Society, 2005), https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4231.
The RFC text and sample implementations are not included.
